course: dictionary
lesson: 6311
title: A mortgage: a loan to buy a home
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mortgage is a big loan from a bank to buy a house or flat. The bank lends the money, and the family pays it back a bit every month for many years. «A mortgage is a huge loan from a bank to buy a home, paid back monthly over about 25 years with interest.» The clues are huge, monthly and 25 years: this is a very big amount, paid slowly over a long time.
explain: Interest is the extra money added on top of a loan. «Because of interest, the total paid back is more than the house cost.» So the family pays back more than the price of the house. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: a loan to buy a home, paid back over years, still makes sense.
explain: Mortgage can also be a verb. To mortgage a house means to use the house as a promise for a loan. If the family cannot pay, the bank can take the house. «Sam's parents mortgaged their house to start a shop» means they used the house as a promise to get the money.
fact: A mortgage is a loan from a bank to buy a home.
fact: You pay back a mortgage a bit every month, often over about 25 years.
fact: Interest is extra money on top of a loan, so you pay back more than you borrowed.
fact: «Mortgage» is also a verb: to mortgage a house means to use it as a promise for a loan.
fact: If payments stop for a long time, the bank can take the home back.
exercise: What is a mortgage? | *A big loan from a bank to buy a home | A free gift from a shop | A small coin for a bus ride
exercise: Why do you pay back more than you borrowed? | Because the bank forgets to count the money | *Because interest is extra money added on top of the loan | Because houses get smaller each year
exercise: «A mortgage is a huge loan from a bank to buy a home.» Find and copy one word that means very big. | *huge | home | buy | bank
test: «Sam's parents mortgaged their house to start a shop.» What does mortgaged mean here? | Sold the house to a neighbour | Lived in the house for free | Painted the house a new colour | *Used the house as a promise for a loan
test: If a family stops paying their mortgage for a long time, what can the bank do? | Nothing, the bank must forget the loan | Pay the family more money | *Take the home back | Give the house to the school
exam: Which clue words in «paid back monthly over about 25 years» help you understand mortgage? | Over and about show the house is small | Paid and back show the bank is happy | Red and blue show the colour of the house | *Monthly and 25 years show a long, slow payment
